From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: enumerate the coded frame sizes

cedrus does not implement VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES, so userspace cannot
tell beforehand how large a picture the engine decodes: the GStreamer
v4l2codecs decoders, which restrict their sink caps to the frame sizes
the driver reports, accept any size, and a stream larger than the
engine decodes is sent to the hardware decoder, where S_FMT clamps the
coded size and every picture is then refused instead of being left to
a software decoder up front.

Report the coded size range of each coded format as a stepwise frame
size: 16x16 to the limits cedrus_max_size() already applies to S_FMT,
in steps of 16 (the coded sizes of all the codecs are multiples of 8 or
16; the display size set through S_FMT is still clamped only). Capture
formats report no sizes: they follow the coded size, there is no scaler,
and v4l2codecs takes capture frame sizes for scaling capabilities.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -415,6 +415,38 @@
 	return cedrus_enum_fmt(file, f, CEDRUS_DECODE_SRC);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Coded formats only: the capture formats follow the coded size (there is
+ * no scaler), and sizes reported for them would be taken for one.
+ */
+static int cedrus_enum_framesizes(struct file *file, void *priv,
+				  struct v4l2_frmsizeenum *fsize)
+{
+	struct cedrus_ctx *ctx = cedrus_file2ctx(file);
+	unsigned int max_width, max_height;
+	struct cedrus_format *fmt;
+
+	if (fsize->index)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	fmt = cedrus_find_format(ctx, fsize->pixel_format, CEDRUS_DECODE_SRC);
+	if (!fmt || fmt->pixelformat != fsize->pixel_format)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	cedrus_max_size(ctx->dev, fmt->pixelformat, &max_width, &max_height);
+
+	fsize->type = V4L2_FRMSIZE_TYPE_STEPWISE;
+	fsize->stepwise.min_width = CEDRUS_MIN_WIDTH;
+	fsize->stepwise.max_width = max_width;
+	fsize->stepwise.step_width = 16;
+	fsize->stepwise.min_height = CEDRUS_MIN_HEIGHT;
+	fsize->stepwise.max_height = max_height;
+	fsize->stepwise.step_height = 16;
+	memset(fsize->reserved, 0, sizeof(fsize->reserved));
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int cedrus_g_fmt_vid_cap(struct file *file, void *priv,
 				struct v4l2_format *f)
 {
@@ -678,6 +710,7 @@
 	.vidioc_s_fmt_vid_cap		= cedrus_s_fmt_vid_cap,
 
 	.vidioc_enum_fmt_vid_out	= cedrus_enum_fmt_vid_out,
+	.vidioc_enum_framesizes		= cedrus_enum_framesizes,
 	.vidioc_g_fmt_vid_out		= cedrus_g_fmt_vid_out,
 	.vidioc_try_fmt_vid_out		= cedrus_try_fmt_vid_out,
 	.vidioc_s_fmt_vid_out		= cedrus_s_fmt_vid_out,
